Subject: ASoC: qcom: q6asm: reset PCM queue and DSP ring on prepare

Adapted from Michael McAllister's upstream submission:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2610.2/14705.html

After an underrun ALSA prepares a new stream, but stale queue/ring indices
can prevent further DSP submissions. Reset them with the new mapping.
A Duo Lite SDL stream reproduced a full buffer with hw_ptr stuck at zero.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -243,6 +243,9 @@
 		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_STOPPED;
 	}
 
+	/* Start every prepared stream at the beginning of its PCM queue. */
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
+
 	ret = q6asm_map_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client,
 				       prtd->phys,
 				       (prtd->pcm_size / prtd->periods),
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
@@ -514,6 +514,8 @@
 
 
 	ac->port[dir].buf = buf;
+	ac->port[dir].dsp_buf = 0;
+	atomic_set(&ac->port[dir].hw_ptr, 0);
 
 	buf[0].phys = phys;
 	buf[0].size = period_sz;
